&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;GAQ427R216&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;While candidates in the listed location(s) are encouraged for this role, candidates in other locations will be considered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks is looking for an exceptional Director, Americas Sales Finance to join the GTM Finance team in the FP&amp;amp;A organization. You will serve as a trusted advisor to Americas Sales and Finance leadership, helping the business make data-driven investment decisions, optimize field capacity, and scale efficiently toward long-term growth and profitability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a finance leader with experience in high-growth environments, you will combine strong business partnership, financial analysis, and executive communication. You will solve ambiguous problems, use first-principles thinking, and translate complex operating data into clear recommendations for senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the strategic Finance partner to Americas Sales leadership, providing financial insight and recommendations on growth priorities, investments, and business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze regional performance against core KPIs, identify risks and opportunities, and translate operating trends into clear executive-level insights, and actions across topline performance and investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales Strategy and Sales Operations to connect operating plans, pipeline, coverage, productivity, and other leading indicators to financial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the Americas perspective into broader GTM and Finance decisions, surfacing regional risks, opportunities, and implications for the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand influence in regional investment decision making, developing analyses and recommendations on trade offs across segments, geographic, coverage models, specialist motions, and other GTM initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a high-performing team and foster strong partnerships across Finance and GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2367&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Business, Economics, Accounting, Finance, or an equivalent quantitative field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant experience in FP&amp;amp;A, corporate finance, management consulting, investment banking, or related roles; experience in enterprise software, SaaS, cloud, or consumption-based businesses strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Partnership: proven ability to build trusted relationships with senior Sales and Finance leaders and influence business decisions through strong financial judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial Modeling: experience building and maintaining complex driver-based financial and operational models independently; advanced Excel or Google Sheets skills required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GTM Acumen: strong understanding of sales capacity, productivity, pipeline, coverage, resource allocation, investment ROI, and operating leverage in a high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Analysis: ability to work with large datasets, identify the most important business drivers, and convert analysis into practical recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: strong executive presence with the ability to simplify complex issues and present compelling narratives, analyses, and recommendations to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People Leadership: demonstrated ability to lead, develop, and retain high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and ownership to solve new problems independently, prioritize effectively, and operate with speed in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
