&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are passionate about enabling data teams to solve the world&#39;s toughest problems — from making the next mode of transportation a reality to accelerating the development of medical breakthroughs. We do this by building and running the world&#39;s best data and AI infrastructure platform so our customers can use deep data insights to improve their business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks SQL (DBSQL) is a serverless data warehouse on the Databricks Lakehouse Platform that lets you run all your SQL and BI applications at scale. The Databricks SQL Control Plane team builds scalable solutions for managing the multi-tenanted DB SQL service. This team creates and maintains services that allow customers to create a data warehouse, scale it within seconds, and run mission critical workloads at scale. &lt;strong&gt;The team is seeking an Engineering Manager to spearhead the development of a new service and architecture for the next generation of our product.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading a team of talented software engineers to build the next-generation low-latency, multi-tenanted, cloud native data warehousing system&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing the team by hiring strong engineering talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading and participating in technical, product and design discussions relating to cloud native database systems&lt;/li&gt;
