&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;GAQ327R292&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a finance function that stays ahead of the curve - leveraging AI, automation, and modern tooling to operate at the pace Databricks demands. We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Global&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Consolidations Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Global Accounting team&lt;/strong&gt; based in India. This is a &lt;strong&gt;foundational hire&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- you will own the end-to-end consolidation and intercompany accounting process across Databricks&#39; 23-entity global footprint, build deep SAP Group Reporting expertise during our S/4HANA implementation, and establish the permanent organisational capability that scales with the business post go-live.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role blends hands-on consolidation execution with technical accounting judgment. As part of the Global Accounting organisation, you will ensure the accurate and timely production of consolidated financial statements under both US GAAP and IFRS, while partnering closely with International Accounting, Corporate Accounting, Tax, and FP&amp;amp;A to drive close integrity across all reporting frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;Own and execute the global consolidation process end-to-end - intercompany reconciliation, elimination entries, currency translation, and multi-entity roll-up across our 23-entity footprint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multi-GAAP close execution, producing parallel US GAAP and IFRS consolidated books each period, identifying and documenting reconciling differences for audit and leadership review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own SAP Group Reporting expertise - serve as the accounting team&#39;s subject matter expert on SAP&#39;s consolidation engine, including configuration, period-end processing, and ongoing optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute intercompany accounting across all entities - ensuring balances are reconciled, disputes are resolved within the close window, and elimination entries are complete and accurate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform monthly consolidation flux analysis, identifying and clearly articulating drivers behind significant period-over-period movements for leadership and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own FX translation and revaluation accounting - functional currency determination, translation adjustments, and CTA reconciliation across all international entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new entity stand-up - partner with Tax, Legal, and International Accounting to establish consolidation processes, intercompany agreements, and reporting structures for new international selling entities as Databricks expands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary point of contact for internal and external audit on consolidation, intercompany, and multi-GAAP reporting matters. Champion compliance with SOX controls across the consolidation process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive AI and automation adoption across consolidation workflows - including automated intercompany matching, elimination entry generation, and reconciliation tooling leveraging the Databricks platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Senior Manager, Close &amp;amp; Consolidation (US) to ensure seamless handoff and time-zone coverage for the most time-sensitive part of the global close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2367&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS Degree with a focus in Economics, Business Administration, Accounting, or Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years progressive accounting experience, with at least 5+ years specifically in consolidation, intercompany accounting, or international accounting within a US multinational framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Chartered Accountant (CA) or CPA equivalent certification is mandatory.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of US GAAP consolidation requirements (ASC 810, ASC 830) and working knowledge of IFRS consolidation standards (IFRS 10, IAS 21). Multi-GAAP reporting experience is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SAP S/4HANA experience required - specifically SAP Group Reporting or SAP BPC. Candidates with implementation experience will be prioritized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing intercompany accounting at scale - reconciliation, netting, dispute resolution, and elimination across a multi-entity, multi-currency environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with FX translation, functional currency assessment, and CTA accounting across complex international structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record driving automation and process improvement in consolidation or close operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting external audits and SOX compliance in a consolidation context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience partnering with remote teams across different geographic areas, including with US-based accounting leadership, and the flexibility to support close timelines that span US Pacific Time hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;GAQ327R195&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Databricks is one of the world’s fastest-growing data and AI companies—an industry leader transforming how organizations harness the power of their data. As we scale rapidly across the globe, we’re seeking an experienced, Global Workplace Services Lead with a focus on events &amp;amp; experiences to develop and drive the overarching strategy, design, and execution for events &amp;amp; experiences across our portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;The Real Estate &amp;amp; Workplace Services (REWS) team operates at an extremely fast pace, and we are in search of a leader with a startup mindset and fresh, innovative ideas to help us scale our events &amp;amp; experiences programming effectively. You will be instrumental in transforming our offices into vibrant community hubs through high-impact programming that builds culture and connection. You’ll also build scalable processes to support on-site business meetings &amp;amp; trainings, off-site experiences for large hubs and departments, and executive gatherings. We need a consistent, scalable approach with a local lens to support our unique cultures in each location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;This role involves cultivating key relationships with third-party partners who are crucial to our expansion and growth. You’ll also collaborate internally with Workplace managers, our inclusion team, ERG leaders, executive admins, our training teams, and many more. The position reports directly to the AMER Workplace services leader with dotted lines to our Workplace leader over EMEA and APJ. This is a full-time, in-office role based in San Francisco, CA. Travel to critical hub locations is required to support the business and build the program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Experience Strategy: &lt;/strong&gt;Define and execute a multi-region workplace experience strategy that drives office attendance, fosters company culture, and strengthens employee community. Include a comprehensive operational roadmap, and timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event Operations &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct and be able to lead and liaise with local workplace specialists and outsourced teams the end-to-end planning and delivery for high-visibility workplace events, including weekly happy hours, monthly activations, business meetings and trainings, executive/board dinners, product launch celebrations, holiday gatherings, and community activations; Command on-site physical events, serving as the primary point of escalation to supervise and manage real-time staffing logistics, and conduct troubleshooting to safeguard attendee safety and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner closely with internal stakeholders—including Internal Communications, People/HR, Executive Assistants, Corporate Marketing, IT/AV, Security, food and beverage teams, and local workplace leaders and specialists—to ensure seamless event delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Stakeholder management: &lt;/strong&gt;Provide exceptional interpersonal, negotiation, and diplomatic capabilities to seamlessly collaborate with, influence, and align global cross-functional stakeholders and executive leadership teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Standards &amp;amp; Playbooks:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop standardized global playbooks, service-level agreements (SLAs), and operational guidelines for local workplace teams to execute events consistently across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Oversee global contracts and relationships with event production vendors, catering teams, and local event suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget &amp;amp; Measurement: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage and build a multi-million-dollar global experience budget. Establish key metrics (NPS or similar, participation rates, cost-per-attendee) to measure event impact, connection, and inform future programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Fluency&lt;/strong&gt;: Approach process and procedure with technical competency utilizing event management platforms, cross-functional collaborative tools (such as Cvent, Asana, Slack, Zoom, Epoch and mobile event applications), and AI to drive production timelines and organize project workforces and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor and Coach: &lt;/strong&gt;Mentor and coach workplace specialists with a focus on events &amp;amp; experiences, as well as outsourced team members to grow in the field, and provide best in class experiences to the Databricks community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2367&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;8–12+ years leading workplace experience, experiential events, or hospitality programs within a fast-growing global tech company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Strong background in planning and driving large-scale, high-budget corporate events and multi-city experiential events on a global scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Be well versed on in-office event execution and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated capacity to independently manage complex logistical operations with concurrent execution timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Deep experience in event production, including technical/AV integration, spatial planning, and high-touch VIP white-glove service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Great communication skills and the ability to draft robust communications plans for events, programs, and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Proven organizational skills, managing multiple work streams and projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Customer focused attitude - ensuring consistently high quality resolutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience working with a mix of outsourced partner teams, vendors, and FTEs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience with procurement, contract management and review, and vendor management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience with google suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience with fresh service, asana, epoch programs preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
