&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Public Sector Field Enablement Manager&lt;/strong&gt; builds the enablement strategy that helps Databricks win new public sector customers, deepen account engagement, and grow platform consumption with a focus on &lt;strong&gt;Federal &lt;/strong&gt;and &lt;strong&gt;National Security.&lt;/strong&gt; This role partners with Sales and Field Engineering leadership to translate public sector priorities into measurable improvements in field readiness, pipeline, ramp, and consumption outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within the first 12–18 months, establish a prioritized public sector enablement roadmap supporting approximately 75 account executives and the field engineers aligned to their accounts, with progress and business impact reviewed in regular leadership business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve public sector field readiness by establishing and increasing adoption of role-specific certifications, skills, and selling behaviors for account executives and solutions architects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce time to productivity for new public sector account executives and solutions architects by establishing repeatable ramp outcomes tied to procurement, compliance, buyer, and Databricks platform knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase enablement-influenced pipeline and public sector consumption attainment by equipping field teams to apply segment-specific account strategies, value narratives, and sales plays in active opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve deal execution in public sector accounts by enabling teams to navigate government procurement vehicles, security requirements, compliance considerations, and competitive positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a measurable feedback loop between the public sector field, business unit leadership, GTM &amp;amp; support teams, and Global Enablement that converts recurring field needs into prioritized programs and scales successful practices into broader enablement motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in sales enablement, revenue enablement, field enablement, sales, or technical pre-sales within the technology sector, including experience supporting both commercial and technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience supporting, selling to, or enabling teams that serve &lt;strong&gt;federal &lt;/strong&gt;or &lt;strong&gt;national security agencies&lt;/strong&gt;, with a practical understanding of public sector procurement, compliance, and buyer decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and operationalize an enablement function or major program from the ground up in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience serving as a trusted advisor to senior Sales and Field Engineering leaders and translating business strategy into prioritized enablement outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written, verbal, storytelling, and presentation skills, including the ability to influence executives and engage large audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A measurement-oriented approach to enablement, with experience connecting readiness, skills, and behaviors to pipeline, consumption, ramp, or other business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI technologies to create, scale, measure, or deliver enablement, along with the ability to build working knowledge of data and AI concepts, Lakehouse architecture, and the Databricks platform.&lt;/li&gt;
