&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and drive execution of strategic security initiatives across Trust &amp;amp; Safety Engineering, Identity and Access Management, Security, and IT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish company-wide processes to identify, track, and resolve high-risk security issues while influencing architecture and infrastructure decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect core security infrastructure to platform services so unified identity, data lineage, and audit controls extend across structured, unstructured, and AI workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve cross-organizational blockers with Director-, VP-, and C-suite engineering leaders while balancing technical tradeoffs and resource constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor TPMs and strengthen standards for technical rigor, operational execution, and program management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Databricks’ security architecture and posture in executive technical reviews and, where appropriate, industry forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or equivalent technical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in technical program management, engineering program management, security program management, or an equivalent technical leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate security, privacy, policy, and compliance objectives into technical strategy, architecture decisions, execution plans, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to resolve conflicting priorities and resource constraints across cross-functional teams without direct authority, establish organization-wide engineering processes, and deliver complex, multi-team roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present complex technical strategies to executive engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-enabled tools to accelerate program strategy, technical problem-solving, analysis, and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite three days per week in Bellevue, Seattle, San Francisco, or Mountain View.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in hyperscale cloud environments such as AWS, Azure, or GCP, or in complex distributed data-processing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior hands-on experience as a software, systems, or security engineer before transitioning to Technical Program Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with unified data governance architectures, distributed-systems security, and or security controls supporting AI and machine-learning infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with external security research, open-source contributions, or speaking at major technical conferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
