&lt;p&gt;P-1607&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Databricks, we are passionate about enabling data teams to solve the world&#39;s toughest problems — from making the next mode of transportation a reality to accelerating the development of medical breakthroughs. We do this by building and running the world&#39;s best data and AI infrastructure platform so our customers can use deep data insights to improve their business. Founded by engineers — and customer-obsessed — we leap at every opportunity to solve technical challenges, from designing next-gen UI/UX for interfacing with data to scaling our services and infrastructure across millions of virtual machines. And we&#39;re only getting started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First-party data collection is the entry point for everything downstream. It also runs on other people&#39;s websites and inside other people&#39;s apps, which raises the bar from a quality, reliability, and development experience. We are looking for an engineer to lead that surface, client and server side.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you&#39;ll have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the collection stack end to end: browser tag, mobile SDKs, server-side endpoints, and the ingest path behind them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the schema and versioning contract, including compatibility across SDK versions already in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead identity handling that spans anonymous and authenticated records, across devices and sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead integrations with other CustomerLake products like Profile &amp;amp; Campaign Agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold hard budgets on page weight, latency, and failure behavior, so that collection never degrades the host application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product management, design, and other engineering teams to build intuitive, scalable, and extensible solutions that drive user &amp;amp; business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering experience, including time as a tech lead, or leading other tech leads, on complex enterprise software projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of an SDK or client library consumed by external developers, including native iOS and Android&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep browser-side JavaScript experience: bundle size, async loading, CSP, storage and cookie restrictions, tracking prevention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-throughput server-side collection: edge endpoints, batching, retries, and delivery guarantees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical grounding in consent and privacy requirements, including regional routing and data minimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership and bias for action in 0→1 environments: you are comfortable making pragmatic trade-offs, operating with incomplete information, and driving projects from idea through launch and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to collaborate across product, engineering, and design teams to align technical strategy with company growth objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combination of technical and people leadership, for example, as a TLM (Nice to have)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a CDP, analytics SDK, or tag management product (Nice to have)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with incident response for code deployed on customer properties (Nice to have)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
